{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If one tries a word with you, can one be weary?</b> — Some say:" "<b>Has one tested</b> — the one who tests. The sense is 'a word with a word.' Others said: for it is the matter itself that tests." "<b>If one tries a word with you, can one be weary?</b> — we cannot refrain from answering you."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra here records that some commentators take the verse as a statement rather than a question.", 2 "The phrase לא נוכל שלא נשיבך is rendered literally as 'we cannot [not answer you]'; the double negative is preserved."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:42.213984848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}